From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi: supply the wifi_utility EEPROM and MAC helpers

ee_flash.c and eeprom.c expect three helpers from MediaTek's wifi_utility
driver: mt_eeprom_read_wifi(), mt_eeprom_write_wifi() and
mt_mac_address_read_wifi().  That driver is not part of this tree, so the
first modpost run of the MT7993 build stopped with

    ERROR: modpost: "mt_eeprom_read_wifi" [mt_wifi.ko] undefined!
    ERROR: modpost: "mt_mac_address_read_wifi" [mt_wifi.ko] undefined!
    ERROR: modpost: "mt_eeprom_write_wifi" [mt_wifi.ko] undefined!

Provide the three functions locally:

- The reference board has no dedicated factory partition (the device tree
  exposes bl2 plus a single ubi volume) and the MT7993 EEPROM image is
  installed as /lib/firmware/MT7993_EEPROM.bin, which
  rtmp_ee_flash_init() loads when the flash ID does not validate.  Report
  the flash access as unavailable instead of inventing a partition name;
  the caller ignores the return value and the BIN fallback takes over.
- Flash writes are not supported on this platform (the vendor driver
  delegates them to ated), so return -EOPNOTSUPP.
- mt_mac_address_read_wifi() returns -ENOENT: there is no device tree or
  NVMEM per-band MAC address, and -ENOENT is the documented "no entry"
  result that leaves the EEPROM address in place without a warning.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt_wifi/hw_ctrl/ee_flash.c
+++ b/mt_wifi/hw_ctrl/ee_flash.c
@@ -30,6 +30,23 @@
 int mt_eeprom_read_wifi(loff_t from, size_t len, u_char *buf);
 int mt_eeprom_write_wifi(loff_t to, size_t len, const u_char *buf);
 
+/*
+ * ponwrt: these two helpers are normally exported by the MediaTek
+ * "wifi_utility" module, which is not part of this tree. The board has no
+ * dedicated factory partition - the whole flash is UBI - so the EEPROM image
+ * comes from /lib/firmware/MT7993_EEPROM.bin instead. Fail the access and let
+ * rtmp_ee_flash_init() fall back to the BIN image.
+ */
+int mt_eeprom_read_wifi(loff_t from, size_t len, u_char *buf)
+{
+	return -ENODEV;
+}
+
+int mt_eeprom_write_wifi(loff_t to, size_t len, const u_char *buf)
+{
+	return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+}
+
 #define flash_read(_ctrl, _ptr, _offset, _len) mt_eeprom_read_wifi(_offset, (size_t)_len, _ptr)
 #define flash_write(_ctrl, _ptr, _offset, _len) mt_eeprom_write_wifi(_offset, (size_t)_len, _ptr)
 
--- a/mt_wifi/hw_ctrl/eeprom.c
+++ b/mt_wifi/hw_ctrl/eeprom.c
@@ -28,6 +28,17 @@
 
 #ifdef HWIFI_SUPPORT
 extern int mt_mac_address_read_wifi(struct device *dev, u32 band_idx, u8 *addr);
+
+/*
+ * ponwrt: the MediaTek "wifi_utility" module that used to provide this
+ * helper is not part of this tree, and the board device tree exports no
+ * per-band MAC address. Report "no such entry" so the caller keeps the
+ * address taken from the EEPROM image, as documented for a failed lookup.
+ */
+int mt_mac_address_read_wifi(struct device *dev, u32 band_idx, u8 *addr)
+{
+	return -ENOENT;
+}
 #endif
 
 struct chip_map {
